WEBVTT

00:00:31.615 --> 00:00:34.826
Ladies and gentlemen,
Conan O'Brien's head.

00:00:36.203 --> 00:00:38.497
- Conan!
- Thank you, thank you.

00:00:39.122 --> 00:00:40.499
Let's get started.

00:00:40.582 --> 00:00:41.875
Max, play me over.

00:00:42.543 --> 00:00:45.045
Looks like someone forgot to feed Max.

00:00:47.381 --> 00:00:51.802
So, people are getting pretty worried
about this Y2K problem, huh?

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:54.972
No, they fixed that 900 years ago.

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:57.057
Just bear with me, sir. Anyway,

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:59.351
- I'm walking to work this morning...
- I doubt it!

00:01:00.485 --> 00:01:03.363
Listen, pal, I may have lost
my freakishly long legs

00:01:03.447 --> 00:01:05.073
in the war of 2012,

00:01:05.157 --> 00:01:07.075
but I've still got something
you'll never have.

00:01:07.159 --> 00:01:08.785
- A soul!
- Eh.

00:01:08.869 --> 00:01:09.953
And freckles.

00:01:14.833 --> 00:01:16.752
Well, I'm out of material.

00:01:16.835 --> 00:01:19.504
You can catch me next week
at the Andromeda Chuckle Hut.

00:01:19.588 --> 00:01:20.797
Enjoy your breakfast.

00:01:24.593 --> 00:01:27.512
Let's face it,
comedy is a dead art form.

00:01:27.596 --> 00:01:29.932
Now, tragedy...

00:01:30.015 --> 00:01:31.183
That's funny.

00:01:31.266 --> 00:01:32.434
Come on, everyone,

00:01:32.517 --> 00:01:37.522
perhaps some skiing will help us forget
the moldy old antics of Conan O'Brien.

00:01:37.606 --> 00:01:38.607
- Yeah!
- Great idea.

00:01:38.690 --> 00:01:39.942
We can only hope.

00:01:41.068 --> 00:01:42.736
This snow is beautiful.

00:01:42.819 --> 00:01:44.905
I'm glad global warming never happened.

00:01:44.988 --> 00:01:46.240
Actually, it did,

00:01:46.323 --> 00:01:48.617
but thank god
nuclear winter canceled it out.

00:01:50.619 --> 00:01:52.871
- Hi.
- Enough of your mindless chitchat!

00:01:52.955 --> 00:01:53.956
Let's get going.

00:01:54.539 --> 00:01:56.291
Damn it, we're stuck!

00:01:56.375 --> 00:01:59.711
At least you're not cold-blooded.

00:02:01.171 --> 00:02:02.881
Sweet Lion of Zion,

00:02:02.965 --> 00:02:04.508
look at the Professor go!

00:02:19.982 --> 00:02:22.317
Look out! We're heading
straight for those trees!

00:02:22.401 --> 00:02:23.819
Yeah, yeah, relax.

00:02:23.902 --> 00:02:25.946
- Trees down.
- Trees down.

00:02:26.863 --> 00:02:29.324
Cool. Hey, what do you do
if you want the trees up?

00:02:29.408 --> 00:02:31.535
Trees up.

00:02:31.618 --> 00:02:33.537
- Trees down.
- Trees down.

00:02:35.122 --> 00:02:37.082
Looking good, beef ball!

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:42.588
Excuse me, sir,
you're snowboarding off the trail.

00:02:42.671 --> 00:02:48.051
Lick my frozen metal ass. Uh-oh.

00:03:05.986 --> 00:03:06.987
Huh?

00:03:09.197 --> 00:03:10.699
You, a bobsledder?

00:03:10.782 --> 00:03:12.367
That I'd like to see.

00:03:12.451 --> 00:03:14.369
Listen, you filthy crab,

00:03:14.453 --> 00:03:18.498
a thousand years ago there was
a legendary team of Jamaican bobsledders.

00:03:18.582 --> 00:03:19.875
Yep, I remember.

00:03:19.958 --> 00:03:21.418
They came in last at the Olympics,

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:23.503
then retired to promote
alcoholic beverages.

00:03:23.587 --> 00:03:26.256
A true inspiration for the children.

00:03:32.221 --> 00:03:34.223
Um, a little help, please!

00:03:34.765 --> 00:03:36.558
No!

00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:47.945
Oh, what the hell.

00:03:56.578 --> 00:03:57.829
You poor man.

00:03:57.913 --> 00:03:59.081
What happened to you?

00:03:59.164 --> 00:04:02.292
Well, there I was
on the triple diamond slope,

00:04:02.376 --> 00:04:03.377
when suddenly...

00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:04.753
Oh, excuse me.

00:04:04.836 --> 00:04:05.963
Hello, there.

00:04:11.593 --> 00:04:13.470
Hmm. Wha...

00:04:17.307 --> 00:04:22.854
Ah! Nothing like a warm fire
and a super soaker of fine cognac.

00:04:24.773 --> 00:04:27.484
Yeah, it really puts you
in the Christmas spirit.

00:04:27.568 --> 00:04:29.069
- What-mas?
- Christmas.

00:04:29.152 --> 00:04:31.822
You know, X-M-A-S.

00:04:31.905 --> 00:04:33.865
Oh, you mean Xmas.

00:04:33.949 --> 00:04:36.410
You must be using
an archaic pronunciation.

00:04:36.493 --> 00:04:38.537
Like when you say "ask" instead of "axe."

00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:41.164
Xmas, huh?

00:04:41.248 --> 00:04:44.334
You know, this will be
my first Xmas away from home.

00:04:44.418 --> 00:04:45.586
Hey, hey.

00:04:45.669 --> 00:04:47.462
Let me axe you something.

00:04:47.546 --> 00:04:50.507
Would it cheer you up
if we went and cut down an Xmas tree?

00:04:50.757 --> 00:04:53.218
Yeah, an old-fashioned Xmas tree.

00:04:53.844 --> 00:04:57.389
- Hey! These aren't Xmas trees!
- Ho-ho-ha?

00:04:57.472 --> 00:04:59.933
They're supposed to be
some kind of, you know, pine tree.

00:05:00.017 --> 00:05:03.604
Pine trees have been extinct
for 800 years, Fry.

00:05:03.937 --> 00:05:05.355
Gone the way of the poodle

00:05:05.439 --> 00:05:08.191
and your primitive notions of modesty.

00:05:09.610 --> 00:05:11.612
Ah! Brisk.

00:05:11.695 --> 00:05:14.072
This isn't the way
Christmas is supposed to be.

00:05:14.323 --> 00:05:15.407
There, there.

00:05:15.490 --> 00:05:16.700
Everything is changed.

00:05:16.783 --> 00:05:18.285
That's not true.

00:05:34.384 --> 00:05:37.930
Oh, Xmas tree,
Oh, Xmas tree

00:05:44.353 --> 00:05:45.354
Ow!

00:05:45.437 --> 00:05:48.857
Every Christmas my mom would get
a fresh goose for goose burgers,

00:05:48.941 --> 00:05:51.235
and my dad would whip up
his special eggnog

00:05:51.318 --> 00:05:52.861
out of bourbon and ice cubes.

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:56.490
This dumb holiday just makes me think

00:05:56.573 --> 00:05:58.242
of all the things I left behind.

00:05:58.325 --> 00:06:00.160
Let's just stop talking about Xmas.

00:06:00.244 --> 00:06:02.246
Happy Xmas, Xmas people!

00:06:02.329 --> 00:06:03.956
Xmas cards have arrived.

00:06:04.039 --> 00:06:05.123
Xmas!

00:06:05.832 --> 00:06:06.959
Amy, there you go.

00:06:07.042 --> 00:06:09.294
Fry, Professor, Zoidberg.

00:06:09.378 --> 00:06:11.129
A mighty haul for Bender.

00:06:11.213 --> 00:06:12.923
Yes! I got the most!

00:06:13.006 --> 00:06:14.383
I win Xmas!

00:06:14.883 --> 00:06:16.718
And last, but not least,

00:06:16.802 --> 00:06:18.554
the sweet flower of the office...

00:06:18.929 --> 00:06:20.973
me, Hermes Conrad.

00:06:23.559 --> 00:06:24.810
Hmm.

00:06:26.853 --> 00:06:29.398
Aw! A picture of my mommy.

00:06:30.399 --> 00:06:33.902
What's this?
A card from my cousin Zoidfarb.

00:06:34.027 --> 00:06:38.532
Instead of "Claus,"
he writes "Claws."

00:06:38.615 --> 00:06:40.701
Now, that's humorous.

00:06:40.784 --> 00:06:43.870
Today's comedians
could learn from this card.

00:07:04.516 --> 00:07:05.726
What's the point of Xmas

00:07:05.809 --> 00:07:08.395
when everyone you know
died a thousand years ago?

00:07:08.896 --> 00:07:10.981
I'm the loneliest person on Earth.

00:07:11.231 --> 00:07:13.358
Hey, Leela, how about
a little sympathy here, huh?

00:07:18.488 --> 00:07:20.574
Yikes! What was that about?

00:07:20.699 --> 00:07:22.993
She's an orphan.

00:07:23.076 --> 00:07:27.039
Yes, and the only one of her species
in all the known universe.

00:07:27.623 --> 00:07:29.207
What a lonely life.

00:07:29.333 --> 00:07:32.794
My god. Poor Leela.

00:07:33.378 --> 00:07:34.671
Hey, buddy.

00:07:34.755 --> 00:07:36.131
Heard you needed cheering up.

00:07:36.214 --> 00:07:38.300
Well, old Bender will make you laugh.

00:07:38.634 --> 00:07:39.760
Look at me, look

00:07:45.224 --> 00:07:47.893
Oh, man, I got to work on my act.

00:07:52.522 --> 00:07:54.191
I feel like a rat.

00:07:54.274 --> 00:07:55.734
Here I am whining like a pig,

00:07:55.817 --> 00:07:58.528
while all along,
Leela was as lonely as a frog.

00:07:58.612 --> 00:07:59.905
I could kick myself.

00:07:59.988 --> 00:08:02.241
- I'll do it for you.
- Ow!

00:08:02.741 --> 00:08:05.744
- Thanks.
- You should be ashamed of yourself, Fry.

00:08:05.827 --> 00:08:09.373
You'd have to be blind not to notice
that Leela is a cyclops.

00:08:09.748 --> 00:08:12.125
- Fry is over there, man.
- Oh?

00:08:15.003 --> 00:08:16.296
Xmas eve,

00:08:16.380 --> 00:08:19.508
another pointless day
where I accomplish nothing.

00:08:22.469 --> 00:08:25.681
The holiday season is a time
of celebration for most,

00:08:25.764 --> 00:08:27.432
but it is also a time to remember

00:08:27.516 --> 00:08:29.935
the tragic suffering
of the less fortunate.

00:08:30.018 --> 00:08:33.272
Earthlings do not yet know
the meaning of suffering.

00:08:36.567 --> 00:08:40.279
Earlier today, I visited a shelter
for down-and-out robots.

00:08:40.696 --> 00:08:43.073
Homeless robots, too poor to afford

00:08:43.156 --> 00:08:46.368
even the basic alcohol they need
to fuel their circuits.

00:08:46.451 --> 00:08:48.078
Is there anything sadder?

00:08:48.161 --> 00:08:51.623
Only drowning puppies
and there would have to be a lot of them.

00:08:53.417 --> 00:08:54.418
Where you going, Bender?

00:08:54.501 --> 00:08:57.588
To volunteer at Liquor Kitchen
for homeless robots.

00:08:57.671 --> 00:08:58.672
Yeah, right.

00:08:58.755 --> 00:09:00.716
As if you ever did anything charitable.

00:09:00.799 --> 00:09:02.217
I'm very generous.

00:09:02.301 --> 00:09:04.094
What about that time I gave blood?

00:09:04.177 --> 00:09:05.929
- Whose blood?
- Some guy's.

00:09:06.805 --> 00:09:10.183
I've got to do something
to show Lela how sorry I am.

00:09:10.267 --> 00:09:12.019
So what's the problem?

00:09:12.102 --> 00:09:15.480
Simply get down on your claws
and do the apology dance.

00:09:17.774 --> 00:09:19.902
So it's left, left, right...

00:09:19.985 --> 00:09:21.695
Wait! I have a better idea.

00:09:21.778 --> 00:09:24.615
I'll go out and get her
the perfect Xmas present.

00:09:24.698 --> 00:09:27.159
Something so great,
she'll never want to be unhappy again.

00:09:28.118 --> 00:09:29.870
Just be back by sundown, man.

00:09:29.953 --> 00:09:31.413
We'll see. I like to haggle.

00:09:31.496 --> 00:09:33.457
You can't stay out on Xmas eve.

00:09:33.540 --> 00:09:35.125
- You'll be killed!
- Say what?

00:09:35.208 --> 00:09:36.293
Good lord!

00:09:36.376 --> 00:09:38.420
He doesn't know about Santa Claus.

00:09:38.503 --> 00:09:40.631
I know about Santa Claus.

00:09:41.340 --> 00:09:44.676
Back in 2801, the friendly robot company

00:09:44.760 --> 00:09:46.887
built a robotic Santa to determine

00:09:46.970 --> 00:09:48.931
who'd been naughty and who'd been nice,

00:09:49.014 --> 00:09:51.099
and distribute presents accordingly.

00:09:51.391 --> 00:09:52.976
But something went wrong.

00:09:53.060 --> 00:09:55.270
Wow, 2801.

00:09:55.520 --> 00:09:57.439
- Anyway...
- Wait, you fool!

00:09:57.522 --> 00:09:59.233
Due to a programming error

00:09:59.316 --> 00:10:01.526
Santa's standards were set too high

00:10:01.610 --> 00:10:04.696
and he invariably judges
everyone to be naughty.

00:10:04.780 --> 00:10:06.281
If he catches you after dark,

00:10:06.365 --> 00:10:09.451
he'll chop off your head
and stuff your neck full of toys

00:10:09.534 --> 00:10:10.953
from his sack of horrors.

00:10:13.789 --> 00:10:15.332
Nice meeting you.

00:10:22.256 --> 00:10:23.674
Welcome, brother.

00:10:23.757 --> 00:10:26.343
May the blessings of the season
be upon you.

00:10:26.426 --> 00:10:27.886
Yeah, yeah, amen.

00:10:27.970 --> 00:10:31.139
Listen, I'm one of those lazy,
homeless bums I've been hearing about.

00:10:31.223 --> 00:10:33.100
Could you point me to the free booze?

00:10:34.768 --> 00:10:35.769
Oh, yeah. Oh, yeah.

00:10:38.397 --> 00:10:41.441
There's this girl who I really like,
but she thinks I'm a jerk.

00:10:41.525 --> 00:10:42.526
Can you help me?

00:10:42.609 --> 00:10:44.695
Yeah, there's a suicide booth
in the food court,

00:10:44.778 --> 00:10:46.488
though there's a line this time of year.

00:10:46.572 --> 00:10:48.073
No, I need to get her a gift,

00:10:48.156 --> 00:10:49.866
and I need it before sundown.

00:10:49.950 --> 00:10:52.369
Well, you can't go wrong
with something traditional.

00:10:52.452 --> 00:10:54.663
A Surface-to-Santa rocket launcher.

00:10:54.746 --> 00:10:56.832
It comes with three
jolly-seeking missiles.

00:10:56.957 --> 00:10:59.042
That's funny.

00:10:59.167 --> 00:11:01.044
Careful, sir.

00:11:06.216 --> 00:11:07.509
Oh, yeah.

00:11:07.593 --> 00:11:10.053
You filthy hobos sure know how to live.

00:11:10.637 --> 00:11:13.557
Hey, chief, someone is stealing
your handkerchief full of crap.

00:11:13.640 --> 00:11:15.934
Hmm?

00:11:16.727 --> 00:11:19.521
Excuse me, sir,
might I have a sip of booze?

00:11:19.980 --> 00:11:21.857
I'm sorry, Tinny Tim,

00:11:21.940 --> 00:11:24.026
seems we ran out early tonight.

00:11:24.109 --> 00:11:26.361
I understand.

00:11:27.029 --> 00:11:30.365
My god, that poor kid.

00:11:30.490 --> 00:11:34.328
You're the last store open.
I need something for my friend Leela.

00:11:41.168 --> 00:11:44.129
- Just give me your best animal.
- Best? Well, that's a matter of opinion.

00:11:44.212 --> 00:11:46.256
I personally like the electric snail.

00:11:47.591 --> 00:11:48.967
That's a stupid animal.

00:11:49.051 --> 00:11:50.052
You're stupid.

00:11:50.135 --> 00:11:51.720
I said I want the best one.

00:11:51.803 --> 00:11:54.264
Now which costs more,
the parrot or the stink lizard?

00:11:54.348 --> 00:11:57.184
The lizards are a buck each,
the parrot is 500 dollars.

00:11:57.309 --> 00:11:59.519
That's a hell of a good parrot.

00:11:59.937 --> 00:12:03.023
Although, I could get 500 lizards
for the same price.

00:12:03.398 --> 00:12:04.942
Girls like swarms of lizards, right?

00:12:05.025 --> 00:12:07.903
Sir, the store is closing in two minutes.

00:12:07.986 --> 00:12:10.072
Okay, okay. I'll take the 500 lizards.

00:12:10.447 --> 00:12:11.448
No, wait.

00:12:11.531 --> 00:12:13.408
Yes. No. Yes.

00:12:13.617 --> 00:12:15.077
Yes. Yes.

00:12:15.410 --> 00:12:16.662
The parrot.

00:12:19.081 --> 00:12:20.999
Well, I spent every penny I had,

00:12:21.083 --> 00:12:24.336
but I bet Leela is going to love you.

00:12:24.419 --> 00:12:27.506
Hey, you're quite the talker, aren't you?

00:12:27.589 --> 00:12:28.715
Shut the hell up!

00:12:29.007 --> 00:12:30.008
Ow!

00:12:31.051 --> 00:12:32.135
Stupid bird!

00:12:32.219 --> 00:12:33.637
I know where you live!

00:12:41.687 --> 00:12:43.188
Hey, it's Leela.

00:12:43.272 --> 00:12:45.065
Sorry I stormed out before.

00:12:45.148 --> 00:12:47.067
I didn't mean to ruin everyone's Xmas.

00:12:47.192 --> 00:12:48.944
Huh? You were gone?

00:12:49.027 --> 00:12:52.489
It's just that I get tired of Fry
always only thinking of himself.

00:12:52.573 --> 00:12:53.615
I hear that.

00:12:53.699 --> 00:12:55.450
I axe him to set the table,

00:12:55.534 --> 00:12:57.869
instead he goes out to buy you a present.

00:12:57.953 --> 00:12:59.079
Selfish dog.

00:12:59.162 --> 00:13:01.039
Wait. You mean he's still out?

00:13:01.123 --> 00:13:02.416
His life's in danger.

00:13:02.499 --> 00:13:04.543
- Why?
- I'm telling you why.

00:13:04.626 --> 00:13:06.795
Santa Claus is coming to town!

00:13:16.555 --> 00:13:17.764
All right, bird,

00:13:17.848 --> 00:13:20.100
you thought you could beat me
in a game of wits,

00:13:20.183 --> 00:13:22.477
but you just met your equal.

00:13:45.500 --> 00:13:47.794
Ah-ha! Cornered.

00:13:56.011 --> 00:13:57.012
Phew!

00:14:00.224 --> 00:14:01.225
Phew!

00:14:05.854 --> 00:14:07.314
- Hi there.
- Leela!

00:14:07.397 --> 00:14:09.816
Oh, my god, you saved my life.

00:14:09.900 --> 00:14:12.402
I am going to get you so many lizards.

00:14:14.571 --> 00:14:16.823
You didn't need to buy me a present, fry.

00:14:16.907 --> 00:14:18.992
I just wanted to do something
to make you happy.

00:14:19.368 --> 00:14:22.871
I mean, I miss my family,
but you never even had a family.

00:14:22.955 --> 00:14:23.956
It's okay.

00:14:24.039 --> 00:14:25.749
You're lonely and I'm lonely.

00:14:25.832 --> 00:14:28.293
But together, we're lonely together.

00:14:29.169 --> 00:14:30.629
Merry Xmas, Leela.

00:14:30.963 --> 00:14:32.172
Merry Xmas.

00:14:32.422 --> 00:14:34.174
Huh?

00:14:35.759 --> 00:14:37.010
Oh, boy!

00:14:37.094 --> 00:14:38.345
It's Santa.

00:14:38.428 --> 00:14:42.808
Ho-ho-ho!

00:14:46.979 --> 00:14:49.356
You've been very naughty, Fry and Leela.

00:14:49.439 --> 00:14:50.816
I checked my list.

00:14:50.899 --> 00:14:51.984
Well, check it twice.

00:14:52.067 --> 00:14:54.903
I perform over 50 mega checks per second.

00:14:54.987 --> 00:14:58.240
You're both naughty for disregarding
each other's feelings.

00:14:58.323 --> 00:14:59.575
But we set things right.

00:14:59.658 --> 00:15:01.994
Fry even risked his life
to get me a present.

00:15:02.077 --> 00:15:04.454
But what about your other coworkers?

00:15:04.538 --> 00:15:09.209
Did either of you ever stop to think
about Dr. Zoidberg's feelings?

00:15:09.293 --> 00:15:10.586
No, I swear.

00:15:10.669 --> 00:15:13.547
Santa has something very special

00:15:13.630 --> 00:15:15.215
in his sack for you two.

00:15:17.551 --> 00:15:19.928
Ho-ho-ho!

00:15:22.973 --> 00:15:26.268
So lock the door and hit the floor

00:15:26.351 --> 00:15:28.645
'Cause Santa Claus comes tonight

00:15:30.022 --> 00:15:31.940
- Go away.
- Whoa, hold on.

00:15:32.024 --> 00:15:35.527
How about inviting us in
for a traditional glass of hard cider?

00:15:35.611 --> 00:15:37.571
Oh, all right,

00:15:37.654 --> 00:15:38.947
but just one glass.

00:15:47.456 --> 00:15:49.875
Okay, that's enough.

00:15:49.958 --> 00:15:52.294
I said that's enough!

00:15:53.211 --> 00:15:54.254
Get her purse!

00:16:06.141 --> 00:16:07.184
Please, let us live.

00:16:07.267 --> 00:16:08.977
We'll put out milk and cookies for you.

00:16:09.061 --> 00:16:11.897
You dare bribe Santa?

00:16:12.147 --> 00:16:14.441
I'm going to shove coal
so far up your stocking

00:16:14.524 --> 00:16:16.026
you'll be coughing up diamonds!

00:16:31.667 --> 00:16:34.294
- We're trapped.
- I never thought it would end this way,

00:16:34.378 --> 00:16:36.338
gunned down by Santa Claus.

00:16:36.421 --> 00:16:37.965
Honestly, I didn't see it coming.

00:16:40.801 --> 00:16:41.969
Good-bye, Fry.

00:16:42.052 --> 00:16:43.178
Good-bye, Leela.

00:16:44.388 --> 00:16:45.514
Hey, look.

00:16:45.806 --> 00:16:47.015
We're under the mistletoe.

00:16:52.854 --> 00:16:56.316
Your mistletoe is no match
for my tow missile.

00:17:06.660 --> 00:17:09.496
Uh, your present may need some assembly.

00:17:09.788 --> 00:17:13.417
On the fourth day of Xmas,
I stole from that lady

00:17:13.500 --> 00:17:15.043
Four family photos

00:17:15.127 --> 00:17:16.628
Three jars of pennies

00:17:16.712 --> 00:17:18.463
Two former husbands

00:17:18.547 --> 00:17:21.717
And a slipper on a shoe tree

00:17:21.967 --> 00:17:23.010
Yep!

00:17:24.052 --> 00:17:25.053
Oh, thank you.

00:17:25.470 --> 00:17:28.015
- Help!
- Somebody help us!

00:17:28.098 --> 00:17:29.224
It's humans.

00:17:29.308 --> 00:17:30.893
Shall we mug them, robot sir?

00:17:30.976 --> 00:17:32.853
No, wait. I know these guys.

00:17:33.103 --> 00:17:34.146
They got nothing.

00:17:35.898 --> 00:17:39.067
Ho-ho-ho!

00:17:39.151 --> 00:17:41.486
You've been very naughty, Bender.

00:17:41.570 --> 00:17:43.322
What, me? I didn't do nothing.

00:17:43.405 --> 00:17:44.573
You're thinking of the kid.

00:17:44.656 --> 00:17:46.450
My god, Bender,

00:17:46.533 --> 00:17:47.743
framing an orphan?

00:17:47.826 --> 00:17:49.411
That's so naughty

00:17:49.494 --> 00:17:52.414
I'll have to add it to my list right now.

00:17:52.915 --> 00:17:54.833
Mm, framing...

00:17:55.876 --> 00:17:58.295
I-N...

00:17:59.129 --> 00:18:00.464
G.

00:18:01.465 --> 00:18:02.466
N...

00:18:04.259 --> 00:18:05.928
Amy, this is for you.

00:18:06.011 --> 00:18:08.680
A set of combs for your beautiful hair.

00:18:08.764 --> 00:18:10.807
Oh, that's so sweet.

00:18:10.891 --> 00:18:12.809
But I sold my hair to a wig maker

00:18:12.893 --> 00:18:15.103
so I could buy a set of combs for Hermes.

00:18:15.187 --> 00:18:16.730
Oh, the irony!

00:18:16.813 --> 00:18:19.608
I sold my hair so I could buy
this third set of combs

00:18:19.691 --> 00:18:20.734
for Zoidberg.

00:18:20.817 --> 00:18:21.818
Thank you.

00:18:21.902 --> 00:18:25.322
These will come in handy for my new hair.

00:18:25.405 --> 00:18:28.659
Finally, I look as pretty as I feel.

00:18:28.742 --> 00:18:30.327
- Help!
- Help!

00:18:30.410 --> 00:18:32.204
Oh, let us in! Help us!

00:18:32.287 --> 00:18:34.081
Oh, help! Oh, no!

00:18:35.457 --> 00:18:38.335
Oh, dear, They'll be killed
on our doorstep,

00:18:38.418 --> 00:18:41.296
and there's no trash pickup
till January 3rd.

00:18:43.465 --> 00:18:44.466
Huh?

00:18:45.551 --> 00:18:47.302
Sweet manatee of galilee,

00:18:47.386 --> 00:18:48.554
he's on the roof!

00:18:50.556 --> 00:18:53.016
Quick! The armor-plated chimney cover.

00:18:54.309 --> 00:18:56.687
Push! Push!

00:18:56.770 --> 00:18:57.980
Use teamwork!

00:19:05.821 --> 00:19:06.822
Oh, dear. Oh, dear.

00:19:11.702 --> 00:19:15.497
You've all been very naughty,
very naughty, indeed.

00:19:15.581 --> 00:19:17.082
Except you, Dr. Zoidberg.

00:19:17.165 --> 00:19:18.292
This is for you.

00:19:18.375 --> 00:19:22.045
A pogo stick. Mm!

00:19:22.129 --> 00:19:23.839
As for the rest of you,

00:19:23.922 --> 00:19:27.175
I'm going to tear off your skin
like wrapping paper

00:19:27.259 --> 00:19:29.845
and deck the halls with your guts.

00:19:29.928 --> 00:19:33.098
Yeah? Well, I don't believe
in Santa Claus.

00:19:33.181 --> 00:19:34.558
Come on, everybody.

00:19:34.641 --> 00:19:36.977
If you don't believe in him,
he can't hurt you.

00:19:37.060 --> 00:19:39.104
Oh, god, the pain!

00:19:39.187 --> 00:19:41.273
Ho-ho-ho!

00:19:41.356 --> 00:19:44.276
Time to get jolly on your naughty asses.

00:19:44.359 --> 00:19:48.280
Ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho!

00:19:48.363 --> 00:19:49.364
Watch out!

00:19:49.448 --> 00:19:52.159
His belly is shaking
like a bowl full of nitroglycerin.

00:19:53.994 --> 00:19:55.120
Rudolph's nose!

00:19:55.203 --> 00:19:56.538
He's going to blow!

00:20:02.461 --> 00:20:03.629
Ah-ha!

00:20:29.613 --> 00:20:31.657
Xmas dinner, everyone.

00:20:33.242 --> 00:20:34.618
Uh, Bender,

00:20:34.701 --> 00:20:36.161
where did you get that bird?

00:20:36.245 --> 00:20:37.829
I found it lying in the street,

00:20:37.913 --> 00:20:39.498
like all the food I cook.

00:20:39.581 --> 00:20:41.041
Dig in, everyone!

00:20:41.124 --> 00:20:42.668
Ugh.

00:20:44.127 --> 00:20:45.128
Thank you, sir.

00:20:45.212 --> 00:20:46.421
You got the toenail.

00:20:53.387 --> 00:20:55.639
- Uh-oh.
- Oh!

00:20:55.722 --> 00:20:57.683
Look, the food isn't what's important.

00:20:57.766 --> 00:20:58.934
I'm so hungry.

00:20:59.017 --> 00:21:00.352
The important thing is

00:21:00.435 --> 00:21:02.145
we are all together for Xmas.

00:21:02.229 --> 00:21:04.231
And even though I'm surrounded by robots

00:21:04.314 --> 00:21:05.899
and monsters and old people,

00:21:05.983 --> 00:21:08.151
I've never felt more at home.

00:21:08.235 --> 00:21:09.361
Hear, hear.

00:21:09.444 --> 00:21:12.322
Now let's all of us shut up and sing.

00:21:13.865 --> 00:21:16.034
He knows when you are sleeping

00:21:16.118 --> 00:21:18.662
He knows when you're on the can

00:21:18.745 --> 00:21:21.290
He'll hunt you down and blast your ass

00:21:21.373 --> 00:21:23.458
From here to Pakistan

00:21:23.584 --> 00:21:25.168
-  Oh 
-  You better not breathe

00:21:25.252 --> 00:21:26.420
You better not move

00:21:26.503 --> 00:21:28.630
You're better off dead
I'm telling you, dude

00:21:28.714 --> 00:21:33.135
Santa Claus is gunning you down!

00:21:36.221 --> 00:21:39.016
Merry Xmas, everyone.

00:22:01.121 --> 00:22:02.456
I'll be back,

00:22:02.539 --> 00:22:04.708
back when you least expect it.

00:22:05.792 --> 00:22:08.670
Next Xmas!

00:22:08.754 --> 00:22:12.174
Ho-ho-ho!